<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#ManagerKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "system (the computer's own), helper (a front end to another manager or to a user repository) or universal (works on many systems)."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#HelperKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#ManagerKind> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Search> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "search"@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#commandOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#PackageName> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#PackageName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What one family calls the package that gives a program: xz-utils on the Debian family and xz on the Arch family, or alternatives (a|b) for releases that renamed it."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Operation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thing a package manager does, named the same for every manager."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#prohibitionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The manager the prohibition is about."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#usesManager> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#commandOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The manager the command belongs to."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Assurance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How far a family has been tried: on a real computer (verified), only against stand-ins (stand-in), not at all (untested), or not applicable (none, for what is only catalogued)."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#PackageName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
