<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#executable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#forProgram> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Program> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Operation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Operation"@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1" .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#needsAdministrator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#detectedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#tier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "required or comfort."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#SystemFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Operating systems that share a package manager and the names of their packages, named in the way a harness detects them: by the ID or ID_LIKE of /etc/os-release, or by the platform where there is none."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#nonInteractive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Command> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#QueryInstalled> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether one package is installed: the exit status answers."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#SupportStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether a harness acts on a family (supported), or only knows of it (catalogued)."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#environment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Assurance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#forbiddenTemplate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Operation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#adminInstall> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The command a person with administrator rights runs to install packages (a pm:template with {packages})."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Refresh> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Operation> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#HelperKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "helper"@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#executable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#prohibitionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#PackageManager> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#verifiedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Where and when it was run for real, in words. Without it, a command, a family or a flag is not verified."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#origin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tier"@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Verified> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Assurance> .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#template> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Its words, separated by spaces, with {packages} (one or more names) or {package} (one) where the names go. No shell syntax: it is run as a list of words."@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Upgrade> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "upgrade"@en .
<https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/packaging#Program> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A program a computer needs, named once, whatever each family calls its package."@en .
